  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033857/assets/dc16f02e1eb47605ae2f21c64fd0f5c2c2bde6526a22d3965da5fa991869524e.png)\n\nConsider the collection of point masses above, where the $x$-coordinates are measured in meters. What is the $x$-coordinate of the center of mass for this system?",
  "worked_solution": "The center of mass, denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{x},$ of a collection of point masses ${m}_{1},{m}_{2},\u2026,{m}_{n}$ located at ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n}$ along the $x$-axis is given by \n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere \n\n- $m={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}$ is the total mass of the system,\n\n- ${M}_{O}={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i}$ is the total moment of the system about the origin $O.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{1} & =7, & \\,{m}_{2} & =4, & \\,{m}_{3} & =1, \\\\ {x}_{1} & =-1, & \\,{x}_{2} & =2, & \\,{x}_{3} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the total mass of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}+{m}_{2}+{m}_{3} \\\\  & =7+4+1 \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand the total moment of the system about the origin is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{O} & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{m}_{i}{x}_{i} \\\\  & ={m}_{1}{x}_{1}+{m}_{2}{x}_{2}+{m}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =7\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-7+8+3 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{O}}{m}=\\frac{4}{12}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$",
